{"id":"3311bfe05245f437","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-thm-roitman.md","title":"Roitman's Theorem","display":"thm-roitman — Roitman's Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-roitman","aliases":["58-thm-roitman"],"display":"thm-roitman — Roitman's Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-albanese-map]]","[[58-df-algebraic-cycle]]","[[58-df-chow-group]]","[[58-df-abelian-variety]]","[[58-df-homomorphism]]","[[58-df-bijective]]","[[58-df-abelian-group]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-roitman"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-roitman</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-roitman — Roitman's Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"41289d25523036d5\" href=\"?note=41289d25523036d5\" title=\"58-df-albanese-map\">58-df-albanese-map</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"53a60793a214598a\" href=\"?note=53a60793a214598a\" title=\"58-df-algebraic-cycle\">58-df-algebraic-cycle</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"9554b584e6760909\" href=\"?note=9554b584e6760909\" title=\"58-df-chow-group\">58-df-chow-group</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"bf0ad86f0f4cd75f\" href=\"?note=bf0ad86f0f4cd75f\" title=\"58-df-abelian-variety\">58-df-abelian-variety</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"f32a973b59a825e4\" href=\"?note=f32a973b59a825e4\" title=\"58-df-homomorphism\">58-df-homomorphism</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"d583890235faf0d5\" href=\"?note=d583890235faf0d5\" title=\"58-df-bijective\">58-df-bijective</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"9f54a13cf4872f4e\" href=\"?note=9f54a13cf4872f4e\" title=\"58-df-abelian-group\">58-df-abelian-group</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,A_0,m_0,e_0,A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}},e_{\\mathrm{Alb}},\\alpha,T_0,T_{\\mathrm{Alb}}\\in V\">\\(X,A_0,m_0,e_0,A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}},e_{\\mathrm{Alb}},\\alpha,T_0,T_{\\mathrm{Alb}}\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SmoothConnectedProjectiveVariety}_{\\mathbb C,S}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{SmoothConnectedProjectiveVariety}_{\\mathbb C,S}:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DegreeZeroChowGroupData}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{DegreeZeroChowGroupData}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AlbanesePointGroupData}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{AlbanesePointGroupData}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AlbaneseCycleMap}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{AlbaneseCycleMap}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> are the typed algebraic-geometry interface predicates for the standard complex constructions</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AbelianGroup}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{AbelianGroup}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GroupHomomorphism}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{GroupHomomorphism}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Bijective}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Bijective}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> are the registered algebraic predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TorsionSubgroup}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{TorsionSubgroup}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> is defined below without an undeclared scalar-multiple operation</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}roitman\\text{-}torsion\\text{-}subgroup}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TorsionSubgroup}_S(T,G,m,e)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{AbelianGroup}_S(G,m)\\land e\\in G\n\\land\\forall g\\in G\\;\\bigl(m(\\langle e,g\\rangle)=g\\land m(\\langle g,e\\rangle)=g\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land T=\\Bigl\\{g\\in G:\\exists n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists s\\in G^{n+1}\\;\\bigl(\ns(0)=e\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{103pt}\\land\\forall k\\in n\\;s(k+1)=m(\\langle s(k),g\\rangle)\n\\land s(n)=e\\bigr)\\Bigr\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}roitman\\text{-}torsion\\text{-}subgroup}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TorsionSubgroup}_S(T,G,m,e)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{AbelianGroup}_S(G,m)\\land e\\in G\n\\land\\forall g\\in G\\;\\bigl(m(\\langle e,g\\rangle)=g\\land m(\\langle g,e\\rangle)=g\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\land T=\\Bigl\\{g\\in G:\\exists n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\exists s\\in G^{n+1}\\;\\bigl(\ns(0)=e\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{103pt}\\land\\forall k\\in n\\;s(k+1)=m(\\langle s(k),g\\rangle)\n\\land s(n)=e\\bigr)\\Bigr\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}roitman}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{SmoothConnectedProjectiveVariety}_{\\mathbb C,S}(X)\n\\land\\mathrm{DegreeZeroChowGroupData}_S(A_0,m_0,e_0,X)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{AlbanesePointGroupData}_S(A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}},e_{\\mathrm{Alb}},X)\n\\land\\mathrm{AlbaneseCycleMap}_S(\\alpha,A_0,m_0,A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}},X)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{GroupHomomorphism}_S(\\alpha,A_0,m_0,A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}})\n\\land\\mathrm{TorsionSubgroup}_S(T_0,A_0,m_0,e_0)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{TorsionSubgroup}_S(T_{\\mathrm{Alb}},A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}},e_{\\mathrm{Alb}})\n\\Bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\mathrm{GroupHomomorphism}_S\n(\\alpha\\upharpoonright T_0,T_0,m_0\\upharpoonright(T_0\\times T_0),T_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}}\\upharpoonright(T_{\\mathrm{Alb}}\\times T_{\\mathrm{Alb}}))\n\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\alpha\\upharpoonright T_0,T_0,T_{\\mathrm{Alb}}).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}roitman}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{SmoothConnectedProjectiveVariety}_{\\mathbb C,S}(X)\n\\land\\mathrm{DegreeZeroChowGroupData}_S(A_0,m_0,e_0,X)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{AlbanesePointGroupData}_S(A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}},e_{\\mathrm{Alb}},X)\n\\land\\mathrm{AlbaneseCycleMap}_S(\\alpha,A_0,m_0,A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}},X)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{GroupHomomorphism}_S(\\alpha,A_0,m_0,A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}})\n\\land\\mathrm{TorsionSubgroup}_S(T_0,A_0,m_0,e_0)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{TorsionSubgroup}_S(T_{\\mathrm{Alb}},A_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}},e_{\\mathrm{Alb}})\n\\Bigr]\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\mathrm{GroupHomomorphism}_S\n(\\alpha\\upharpoonright T_0,T_0,m_0\\upharpoonright(T_0\\times T_0),T_{\\mathrm{Alb}},m_{\\mathrm{Alb}}\\upharpoonright(T_{\\mathrm{Alb}}\\times T_{\\mathrm{Alb}}))\n\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\alpha\\upharpoonright T_0,T_0,T_{\\mathrm{Alb}}).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The source, both operations and identities, the induced Albanese map, both torsion subsets, the restricted homomorphism, and bijectivity are explicit arguments.  Torsion is defined by finite iteration of the displayed group operation.</li>\n<li>The four algebraic-geometry interface predicates name the standard constructions at the resolution currently available in this book.  In particular, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"9554b584e6760909\" href=\"?note=9554b584e6760909\" title=\"58-df-chow-group\">58-df-chow-group</a> is an affine/codimension presentation with external divisor data and does not by itself define projective <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"CH_0(X)^0\">\\(CH_0(X)^0\\)</span>; this theorem no longer pretends that its zero-argument notation does so.</li>\n<li>For a smooth connected projective variety over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb C\">\\(\\mathbb C\\)</span>, Roitman's theorem identifies the torsion subgroup of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A_0(X)=CH_0(X)^0\">\\(A_0(X)=CH_0(X)^0\\)</span> with the torsion subgroup of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Alb}(X)(\\mathbb C)\">\\(\\operatorname{Alb}(X)(\\mathbb C)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Bloch's conjecture for a smooth projective surface with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_g=0\">\\(p_g=0\\)</span> predicts that the Albanese map on degree-zero zero-cycles is an isomorphism; it does not assert that all zero-cycles are trivial.</li>\n<li>No conclusion that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"CH_0(X)\\otimes\\mathbb Q\\cong\\mathrm{Alb}(X)\\otimes\\mathbb Q\">\\(CH_0(X)\\otimes\\mathbb Q\\cong\\mathrm{Alb}(X)\\otimes\\mathbb Q\\)</span> follows merely from a positive-dimensional <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A_0(X)\">\\(A_0(X)\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-albanese-map","status":"resolved","id":"41289d25523036d5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-albanese-map]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-algebraic-cycle","status":"resolved","id":"53a60793a214598a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-algebraic-cycle]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df